[COMMENTS]
STATION,Crump weir of reinforced concrete and local stone with phosphor bronze crest. Reservoirs in catchment affect runoff. GENERAL: Crump weir of reinforced concrete and local stone with phosphor bronze crest, 10.67m wide. STATION HYDROMETRY: Limited u/s shoaling and weed growth on weir may affect low flows. Fish counter on d/s side of weir not thought to affect performance. Flows contained up to 2.27m. No bypassing on either bank at high flows - channel contained by road wall on lb. Three peak flow ratings applied across period of record. NRW confirm no high flow gaugings; highest gauging at 7.6 cumecs. Reservoirs in catchment affect runoff. FLOW RECORD: Gap in data between 1985 and 1988. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9).
CATCHMENT,Impermeable, predominantly Old Red Sandstone conglomerates, sandstone and marl. Predominantly grassland for livestock farming, significant heathland and some afforestation.
Qmed Suitability,Although not gauged to within 30% of QMED, rating has been extended using a hydraulic model.
Pooling Suitability,Few high flow gaugings. Rating cannot be validated beyond QMED.
[END]
